Hello All,

It is acceptable to use an electrofusion coupling to fuse two pipes with di=
fferent DR=92s.  For instance DR17 to DR11.

In fact it is preferred that an electrofusion coupling is used to fuse two =
different DR=92s together rather than butt fusing.

Recall that there is a limit with the Nupi that the standard fusion cycle n=
ot be used on pipe thinner than DR17.  See Info Blurt #5.

John

--_000_9B7E2735CEC37E4D9137A9548F21D78372545FCA06MAIL_
